@* The action footer shared by the project, scope, test case and defect forms — so placement and
   styling can't drift between them:

     ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     [ Save changes ]  [ Cancel ]                 [ 🗑 Delete test case ]

   Save (the only green fill) far left where the eye lands after the fields, Cancel beside it,
   Delete (the only red, outlined) far right, away from Save. Delete opens a ConfirmDeleteDialog;
   with DangerZone it's left out here and the page shows a DangerZone section instead (deletes that
   cascade). Sticky, so Save stays in view on long forms. form-actions.js adds: Save disabled until
   something changes (RequireChanges), an unsaved-changes warning on Cancel / leaving, ⌘/Ctrl+Enter
   to save and Esc to cancel. Render it as the last thing inside the form (inside the card, or
   Standalone as its own bar when the form spans several cards). *@
<div class="@ContainerClass" data-form-actions
     data-require-changes="@(RequireChanges ? "true" : null)" data-start-dirty="@(StartDirty ? "true" : null)">
    <button type="submit" class="btn-primary" data-form-save name="@SaveName" value="@SaveValue"
            aria-keyshortcuts="Control+Enter Meta+Enter">@SaveLabel</button>
    <a href="@CancelHref" class="btn-outline" data-form-cancel aria-keyshortcuts="Escape">Cancel</a>
    @if (DeleteDialogId is not null && !DangerZone)
    {
        <button type="button" class="btn-danger-outline ml-auto" data-dialog-open="@DeleteDialogId">
            <TrashIcon />@DeleteLabel
        </button>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string SaveLabel { get; set; } = "Save changes";

    /// <summary>Optional name/value posted with Save (the project form dispatches on Model.Op).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? SaveName { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? SaveValue { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string CancelHref { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>The ConfirmDeleteDialog this form's Delete opens; null = no delete (e.g. creating).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? DeleteDialogId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string DeleteLabel { get; set; } = "Delete";

    /// <summary>The delete cascades to other records: leave it out of the footer (the page renders
    /// a DangerZone below the form instead).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool DangerZone { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Keep Save disabled until a field changes (edit forms).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool RequireChanges { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The form already differs from what's saved — e.g. re-rendered after a post-back
    /// (validation error, adding a link row) — so Save starts enabled and leaving warns.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool StartDirty { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The form spans several cards: render as its own card-like bar rather than as the
    /// bottom edge of the card it sits in.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Standalone { get; set; }

    private string ContainerClass => Standalone
        ? "card sticky bottom-0 z-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 !py-4 shadow-md"
        // ! on the margins: the card's space-y-* resets its children's margins and would win, leaving
        // the card's bottom padding showing under the footer.
        : "sticky bottom-0 z-10 -mx-6 !-mb-6 !mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 rounded-b-lg border-t border-gray-200 "
          + "bg-white/95 px-6 py-4 backdrop-blur dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900/95";
}
